From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: validol1979-ops <225744605+validol1979-ops@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:23:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] gemma4: Gemma 4 on S = 2 / 4 slices (Qwen3 sharding, KV
 replication, per-slice fit)

Spec.check allows S > 1 (n_kv % S == 0 or replicated KV heads, H / F / vocab per slice) and refuses
multi-slice MoE, k_eq_v and differing global KV heads with a clear message. Image: per-slice q / KV
(one head when replicated) / wo rows / F / vocab head shard, replicated embedding gather table and
PLE projections, FFN padded to S x the down quantum; build returns S images; descriptors(sid) and every
compile entry point trace each slice. Attention y = all_gather(dot(all_gather(o), wo_loc)) and MLP
y = all_gather(swiglu_down(...)) before the sandwich norms; wpp sharded + all_gather. emulated_logits(S=);
automatic format / PLE placement against the per-slice DRAM (E4B at S = 4, 2 GiB a slice: host int8 PLE,
fp4 layers / head 1.1 GB a slice; every on-card PLE variant exceeds 2 GiB). layouts.head_parallel_indices.
Tests: tests/test_gemma4_slices.py (tiny Gemma 4 at S = 2 / 4, int8 / fp4: resident == static, chunked
prefill, cosine > 0.99 vs emulation, greedy == host, byte-identical KV replicas, host PLE, fit);
tests/test_gemma4.py + slices 69 passed, 4 skipped; test_config_matrix 39 passed (S = 2 Gemma no longer
refused). Codex gpt-6-astra (high), reviewed; full E4B on the card not yet run.

